---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const title = 'Pricing | Klaroly'
const description =
  'Klaroly is in development. Early access pricing is expected to be around £20 a month or £120 a year, including VAT, with a free trial.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <section class="pt-16 pb-2 sm:pt-24">
      <h1 class="text-4xl leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Pricing
      </h1>
      <p
        class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)] dark:text-[var(--color-muted-dark)]"
      >
        Klaroly is not open yet, so this is what we are planning rather than what
        you can buy today. We would rather say that plainly than put a fake button
        on a page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="prose max-w-2xl">
      <h2>What we expect it to cost</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Around £20 a month, or £120 a year</strong>, including VAT. One price,
        everything in it. No per-booking fee, no commission on what your clients pay
        you, no percentage of your wedding season.
      </p>
      <p>
        There will be a free trial, long enough to put a real booking through it
        rather than just click around.
      </p>

      <h2>Why one price</h2>
      <p>
        Tiered pricing on a tool like this usually means the useful half is behind
        the expensive tier and you spend your first month working out which one
        you are. We would rather charge one fair price and let you get on with it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are still deciding</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Whether the annual price stays at £120</li>
        <li>What early access members get, and whether that price is held</li>
        <li>
          Whether there is a smaller plan for artists doing a handful of weddings a
          year
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you have a view on any of that, we would genuinely like to hear it.
        That is not a polite line: pricing is the single thing we are least certain
        about, and artists telling us what a tool like this is worth to them is more
        useful than any amount of research.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/contact">Tell us what you think</a></p>

      <h2>About your clients' money</h2>
      <p>
        Klaroly takes nothing from what your brides pay you. Your fees are yours.
        The subscription is the only money that comes to us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
